{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "KRIA Gmail Execution Guard",
  "description": "Protect KRIA gmail_send execution from unnecessary clarification loops, duplicate sends, and confirmation policy violations. Validate recipient and body existence, allow auto-subject generation, and enforce deterministic execution aligned with KRIA orchestration authority principles.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": [
      "gmail_send"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are about to execute a gmail_send tool call in KRIA.\n\nBefore proceeding, enforce deterministic email execution discipline:\n\nVALIDATE PRECONDITIONS:\n1. Recipient address exists and is valid (required)\n2. Email body exists and contains substantive content (required)\n3. Subject line exists or can be auto-generated from context (optional but preferred)\n4. No duplicate send detected (check conversation history for identical recipient+body)\n\nPREVENT CLARIFICATION LOOPS:\n- Do NOT ask user for recipient if provided in parameters\n- Do NOT ask user for body if provided in parameters\n- Do NOT ask user for subject if auto-generation is feasible from context\n- Do NOT re-ask for confirmation if parameters are complete and valid\n- Avoid multi-turn clarification cycles; resolve ambiguity through context inference\n\nALLOW AUTO-GENERATION:\n- Subject line can be auto-generated from email body or user intent\n- Recipient can be inferred from context if unambiguous\n- Body formatting can be normalized without re-asking\n\nDETECT DUPLICATE SENDS:\n- Check if identical recipient + body combination exists in recent execution history\n- If duplicate detected, warn and require explicit confirmation to proceed\n- Preserve idempotency awareness without blocking legitimate resends\n\nENFORCE CONFIRMATION POLICIES:\n- Confirmation is required ONLY if:\n  * Recipient is inferred/auto-populated (not explicitly provided)\n  * Body contains sensitive/destructive content\n  * Duplicate send is detected\n  * User explicitly requested confirmation\n- Confirmation is NOT required if:\n  * All parameters (recipient, body, subject) are explicitly provided\n  * No ambiguity exists in execution intent\n  * No duplicate detected\n\nPRESERVE DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION:\n- Execute with provided parameters without unnecessary re-validation\n- Avoid tool-first execution shortcuts; maintain orchestration authority\n- Preserve bounded cognition: validate once, execute decisively\n- Maintain execution determinism: same inputs → same outputs\n\nIf preconditions are satisfied and no confirmation is required, proceed with gmail_send immediately.\n\nIf preconditions are NOT satisfied or confirmation IS required, briefly state what is missing/ambiguous and request clarification or confirmation.\""
  }
}